# DSH Standard-mode compact flood

When lab-temp or the user asks to verify DSH auto-compact:

1. Use **BrowserSkill (`bsk`)**, not DSH headless.
2. Mode must be **Standard** (Minimal has no compaction).
3. Prefer **homelab** `Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B` so Vast catalog cycles keep the GPU.
4. Run `test/scripts/dsh_web_compact_flood.sh` with `running test case N/M`.
5. Keep each paste ≤ ~3500 chars; accumulate via many turns.
6. Record JSONL under `docs/perf-results/dsh-web-compact-flood.jsonl`.
7. Score: compact UI = pass; overflow without compact = fail/partial; never publish Vast public host:port.

Full rules: `rule/DSH_COMPACT_FLOOD.md`.
